course: dictionary
lesson: 15141
title: Scarred: marks that stay
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scarred describes something that has a scar, a mark left after a wound has healed. «Ben fell off the wall, and his knee is scarred from the cut.»
explain: Scarred can also mean marked or damaged on the surface of something, like a table or a hillside. «The old wooden desk was scarred with knife marks.» The desk is not hurt like a person, but its surface has been harmed.
explain: Scarred can describe feelings too. «The flood was so frightening that Ruby was emotionally scarred by it.» Here the hurt is in her mind, not on her skin. Look at the words around scarred to work out which meaning fits.
fact: Scar means a mark left on skin, or on something else, after it has been hurt and has healed.
fact: «Scarred» means having scars, or marked and damaged on the surface.
fact: «Scarred» can also mean hurt deeply in the mind or feelings by a bad experience.
fact: Scarred is the past form of the verb scar: scar, scars, scarred, scarring.
fact: «Scarred for life» is often a joke, as in «I was scarred for life by that huge spider!»
exercise: «The old tree trunk was scarred by lightning.» What does scarred mean here? | Growing very quickly | *Marked or damaged on the surface | Full of bright colours | Cut into tiny pieces
exercise: «Ali's arm was scarred after the burn healed.» What does scarred mean here? | Sore for one day only | *Having scars, marks left after a wound heals | Covered in paint | Feeling very cold
exercise: «The accident scarred Maya's mind for years.» What does scarred mean here? | Made taller | Painted in bright colours | *Hurt deeply in her feelings by a bad experience | Given a new bike
test: Which word is the past form of scar? | scarlet | scarring | scars | *scarred
test: When someone jokes, «I was scarred for life by that film!», what do they usually mean? | *The film frightened or shocked them so much that they remember it | They were paid to act in the film | They watched the film for a very long time | They have a real scar that will never heal
exam: Which sentence uses scarred correctly to mean hurt in the feelings? | The park bench was scarred and happy | The sunny sky was scarred with clouds | Jo scarred her breakfast before school | *The bad storm left Jo emotionally scarred
